# Copy this file to .env (cp .env.example .env) and fill in the values on YOUR computer only.
# .env is in .gitignore: it never goes to GitHub. This example file holds names, never real values.
#
# The website (website/) needs NO secret keys today: the Tally order form, the Square payment link and the
# Zelle email are public on purpose — customers need them. Any key written into website/ files would be
# public to everyone, .env or not, because GitHub Pages serves those files as they are. Keys belong only
# in a server or a script that runs on your computer — never in the website.
#
# Before you create a key anywhere, cap what a leaked key could cost (see website/README.md, "Keys and spend
# limits"): e.g. a $10 monthly spend limit on its own workspace / project.

# Claude API (console.anthropic.com) — key from a workspace with a $10 monthly spend limit
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Add others the same way, one per line, e.g.:
# KLAVIYO_PRIVATE_API_KEY=
# SQUARE_ACCESS_TOKEN=
